                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9ef67535-bc7b-41a0-8012-e42c772a5aa5",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff35c4-5a9a-3eb4-9250-3fa684f75f52",
                        "source_sense_id": "19e15ba1-8834-383c-a20b-d3f0c51ca399",
                        "target_lang_word": "unwarily",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "unwarily",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                        "entry_id": "a35a0d6c-ac5c-35d5-b650-08368db7e02c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an unwary manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31bceb18-672b-452f-a6fd-94d316b969fe",
                                                "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                                "text": "One day as I vnvvarily did gaze / on thoſe fayre eyes my loues immortall light: / the vvhiles my ſtoniſht hart ſtood in amaze, / through ſvveet illuſion of her lookes delight."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d89870e-6477-474b-9e6d-f79051859ca8",
                                                "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                                "text": "For in a night the best part of my power, / As I upon advantage did remove, / Were in the Washes all unwarily / Devoured by the unexpected flood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c9bff20-addb-4d53-90fd-6f22ac2c35b1",
                                                "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                                "text": "Not that licence and levity and unconsented breach of faith should herein be countnanc’t, but that some conscionable, and tender pitty might be had of those who have unwarily in a thing they never practiz’d before, made themselves the bondmen of a luckles and helples matrimony."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbc2d706-28e2-4c6e-80ac-7a1abfe389c1",
                                                "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                                "text": "Th’ Ambitious Youth, too Covetous of Fame, / Too full of Angels Metal in his Frame, / Unwarily was led from Vertues ways, / Made Drunk with Honour, and debauch’d with Praise."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c45bcbd7-0988-47aa-9580-1b549b75bdf9",
                                                "sense_id": "05827799-1d07-3ad3-b648-8398d84e3a19",
                                                "text": "[…] the rest of the morning was easily whiled away, […] in dawdling through the green-house, where the loss of her favourite plants, unwarily exposed, and nipped by the lingering frost, raised the laughter of Charlotte […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "24d81cf2-dcf7-4863-844a-ab3d3adb272c",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff35c4-5a9a-3eb4-9250-3fa684f75f52",
                        "source_sense_id": "19e15ba1-8834-383c-a20b-d3f0c51ca399",
                        "target_lang_word": "incautiously",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "incautiously",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8049a922-afaa-3e01-b26a-74ca6f29fcab",
                                        "entry_id": "00fcace8-3f31-3f44-a9bd-78a551fd0cd1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an incautious manner; with a lack of caution."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5d46940-1cc0-4a26-8f4b-983284f8c92c",
                                                "sense_id": "8049a922-afaa-3e01-b26a-74ca6f29fcab",
                                                "text": "His behaviour to herself could now have had no tolerable motive; he had either been deceived with regard to her fortune, or had been gratifying his vanity by encouraging the preference which she believed she had most incautiously shewn."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2463dc58-dfdf-492e-bcb7-6f7b9fa99f5c",
                                                "sense_id": "8049a922-afaa-3e01-b26a-74ca6f29fcab",
                                                "text": "[…] the piranhas habitually attack things much larger than themselves. They will snap a finger off a hand incautiously trailed in the water […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1147b0fc-c0f6-43bd-82b9-a91ca1314041",
                                                "sense_id": "8049a922-afaa-3e01-b26a-74ca6f29fcab",
                                                "text": "The parson explained that the dissenters were insufficiently grounded in religious learning, inappropriately eager to administer the sacraments without his help or sanction, and incautiously emotional in their worship."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "82ae1603-e8fe-40b9-960f-20c81cc9d044",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff35c4-5a9a-3eb4-9250-3fa684f75f52",
                        "source_sense_id": "19e15ba1-8834-383c-a20b-d3f0c51ca399",
                        "target_lang_word": "imprudemment",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "imprudemment",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d16983c9-6dfe-3b68-8794-bee8d1c7c250",
                                        "entry_id": "3dd05cb9-bb0c-31b4-ae72-15c2627ec064",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Avec imprudence."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ef01ddd-6712-4b23-a976-b8776ac071cd",
                                                "sense_id": "d16983c9-6dfe-3b68-8794-bee8d1c7c250",
                                                "text": "De sorte que désormais il faut que je prenne soigneusement garde de ne prendre pas imprudemment quelque autre chose pour moi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "805d986a-d1fe-4011-8da8-3b948b221115",
                                                "sense_id": "d16983c9-6dfe-3b68-8794-bee8d1c7c250",
                                                "text": "L'élevage des vers à soie « ne paie plus ». Voilà pourquoi, aujourd'hui, dans le Gard, on arrache les mûriers : on les remplace imprudemment par des vignes...."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e0f05fd-108f-44cb-8d96-ca2f99134898",
                                                "sense_id": "d16983c9-6dfe-3b68-8794-bee8d1c7c250",
                                                "text": "La cour d’appel partagea alors les dommages, selon les principes de la faute commune, constatant que la victime s’était imprudemment aventurée sur un boulevard passager, sans prendre les précautions nécessaires."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
